From: Erhan Bilgili <erhan.bilgili@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 17:07:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] gamefixes: Hide Wine exports for The Witcher 3.

The updated game checks for wine_get_version before initializing
Streamline and disables frame generation when Wine is detected.

Set HideWineExports under AppDefaults for witcher3.exe in the game's
prefix. Leave other executables and the prefix-wide policy unchanged.
Use the registry helper directly without invoking winetricks.

This also bypasses the game's Wine-based ray-tracing restriction. It
does not fix the underlying ray-tracing crashes.

Link: https://github.com/nanomatters/proton-cachyos/issues/71
---
 gamefixes-steam/292030.py | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 gamefixes-steam/292030.py

diff --git a/gamefixes-steam/292030.py b/gamefixes-steam/292030.py
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/gamefixes-steam/292030.py
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+"""Game fix for The Witcher 3."""
+
+from protonfixes import util
+
+
+def main() -> None:
+    """Allow the game's Wine-gated Streamline initialization."""
+    util.regedit_add(
+        r'HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Wine\AppDefaults\witcher3.exe',
+        'HideWineExports',
+        'REG_SZ',
+        'Y',
+    )
